sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R2-R4, swamp-tasks-model. Nick 2026-11-06: a task VM never holds a GitHub credential; the push step mints its token when it runs, not at admission (an installation token lives one hour). docs/reference/tasks.md#publish-an-external-group.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 16 (no tip read: a push without force refuses a divergent tip and pushes nothing for an identical one); rule 22 (no shipped scripts: task VM work is `@swamp/ssh exec` argv, 209 work is inline `git` and `gh api`; one workspace check, since import checks the bundled commit and tree).
  %% Task copy (2026-11-14): a group whose workspace is a task copy exports through its container's workspace phase; the push stays on the worker. The .env Orbit wrote never leaves a copy: the range from the copy's start is checked before the mint. docs/reference/tasks.md#task-copy.
  %% Task group modes (ADR 0257): a copy group's done check publishes without --check, by a person's release or by the task:pr-when-done tick (docs/cli/task/pr-when-done.mmd), with the same admission and run. docs/reference/tasks.md#task-group-modes.
  %% Base (2026-11-14): a copy's run fetches the default branch into its scratch repository after the mint and before the push, states the checked base, how far it is behind and the overlapping paths, and refuses only a real merge conflict. It reads only intent keys the publish already has. docs/reference/tasks.md#the-base-of-a-copy-publish.
  %% Workflows (2026-11-16): the workflow judgement moved from the copy check to the base read, against the real default head that the publish fetches, not the copy's own remote refs (Operation 24405): a commit that head holds, synced or carried in by hand, is never a change of the copy. It is the net tree diff of `.github/workflows/` between that head and the candidate, the comparison GitHub makes, not the copy's commits (Operation 24460): a copy behind a workflow change of the head refuses too. docs/reference/tasks.md#the-base-of-a-copy-publish.
  %% Own change, merge at publish (2026-11-16, group 5429): a workflow change merged on main after the copy's sync refused copies (#3867), so only the copy's own change refuses: the workflow paths it changed since the merge base (`git diff head...candidate`). GitHub still judges the pushed tree against the default branch (Operation 24460), so a copy only behind a workflow change publishes through a clean merge the worker makes at publish, `Merge main <sha> at publish`; a republish adds the earlier publish merge as a third parent, so its push is a fast-forward. docs/reference/tasks.md#merge-main-at-publish.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: task:publish
  %% kind: tasks.publish
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: task:publish 42<br/>--check=17
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit task:publish 42 --check=17`
  %%> - syntax: `[task] [--check=ID [--title=TEXT --body=TEXT [--draft]]] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the task group, and the passed handoff check whose commit is published
  %%> - optionally a title and body together, to open or update the pull request; without them it only pushes
  %%> - a task copy's group may omit `--check`, `--title` and `--body`: the release of its done check, with the reviewer's title and body, as a ready pull request; on a group that has its pull request, the release pushes its done check again and updates the pull request's title and body with the reviewer's text when its newest turn sent one for that check, else it only pushes
  %%> - a task copy's `--check` without `--title` and `--body`, on a group without a pull request: when the check is the reviewed done check with the reviewer's text, the same Operation opens the pull request, as the release does; any other check only pushes
  %%> - a task copy's `--check` without `--title` and `--body`, on a group that has its pull request: when the check is the done check with the reviewer's text, the same Operation updates the pull request with it, as the release does; any other check only pushes
  Note over GW: Check the candidate<br/>task #5165 · record the key names
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - group 42 is an open external group with its own task copy whose container runs (`tasks.instance_not_running`) and has a start commit; a group without a task copy gets `tasks.no_workspace`: task VM workspaces are removed
  %%> - a task copy's Project is released for publishing: a nested-fleet Project, such as the Orbit Project, or listed in the Gateway's `ORBIT_TASKS_COPY_PUBLISH_PROJECTS`; otherwise HTTP 409 `tasks.copy_publish_held`, and the checked commit stays in the copy
  %%> - a task copy has no earlier turn that may still run (`tasks.copy_turn_unended`)
  %%> - a task copy's last completion did not fail (`tasks.copy_completion_failed`, with its Operation, failed step, error code and the retry `orbit instance:complete ID`), and the copy is `active` (`tasks.copy_not_ready`)
  %%> - check 17 passed for group 42, and required hosted CI passed on its commit, else `tasks.commit_not_checked`
  %%> - without `--check`: the group's work is done, else `tasks.not_done`, also on a group that has its pull request; the done check is the check, and the request is the same from here on (docs/reference/tasks.md#when-the-work-is-done)
  %%> - without `--check`, on a group without a pull request: the reviewer thread's newest turn sent its pull request text on the done check, else `tasks.pr_text_missing`; that text is the title and body, with `Closes #N` added for a group that names issue N and whose body does not close it (docs/reference/tasks.md#the-reviewers-pull-request-text)
  %%> - no other task runs on group 42; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> - a release, and a `--check` that takes the reviewer's text: the done check is read again under the group lock, else `tasks.not_done`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the repository, default branch, commit, checked tree and the copy Node's SSH target
  %%> - for a task copy: its Node's SSH target, its container, its start commit and the path of the `.env` Orbit wrote, from the Instance's record
  %%> - names two `task-publish-token-<uuid>` vault keys for the token and the Git authorization header; it mints and writes no value at admission
  %%> - the `task:pr-when-done` tick admits through this same step, keyed `pr-when-done:<group>:<check>`; its refusal is stored on the group as the publication's error code
  %%> - a copy's `--check` that only pushes records why no pull request opens, `pull_request_withheld`, on the Operation; the run's intent does not carry it
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5165 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the commit, tree, branch `task-42`, default branch and the optional title and body
  %%> - the vault key names of the token and Git authorization header, never their values; no token exists yet
  %%> - for a task copy: the `.env` the Gateway renders from the Instance's stored values, as the vault copy `task-publish-environment-<operation>`; the agent cannot change it
  %%> - for a copy in the nested-fleet project: the Club key's one vault entry `nested-fleet-club-api-key`, which every nested start reads, when the Gateway holds a key
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5165
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  Note over SW: Create publication scratch
  %%> How:
  %%> - a private worker directory holds the bundle, bare repository and bounded CLI replies
    SW->>N: Preflight the copy
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase reads the checkout as `agent` in the container through its Node; HEAD must be the checked commit
    SW->>N: Export the copy
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase bundles the branch as `agent`, checks its head and tree against the candidate, and fetches it to this worker; the Node keeps no copy
    %%> - the phase runs as the behavior `task-workspace-NODE-GROUP` for up to 1,800 s, so a publish of another group's copy on this Node never waits for its lock; the content check, import and push name their group too
    %%> - the Node also pulls the copy's `.env` as a regular file and fetches it beside the bundle; its bytes enter no result or log
    %%> - and the copy's proposed pull request body for the task branch, `.git/orbit/proposed-pr-bodies/task-GROUP.md`, when it is a regular file of at most 64 KiB: data, never run; without it the publish sends the caller's text
    SW->>N: Check the copy
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase `scan` runs `task_copy_scan.py` in the container as root; root reads the copy's secrets, Git runs as `agent` (docs/reference/tasks.md#the-copy-check)
    %%> - the secrets: the Club key in `/run/orbit-club`, the operator WireGuard key, and of each inner machine its Gateway `.env` values, Swamp tokens, Orbit tokens and WireGuard keys; values under 16 bytes and values the start tree holds are skipped and counted
    %%> - every object new from the copy's start to the candidate, and the proposed body, are searched for each value and for a private key block with a real body
    %%> - the evidence names paths, lines, secret names and the digest of the objects read, never a value; a nested-fleet copy without its inner machines is unchecked
    SW->>SW: Read the copy check
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data reads the evidence: a secret refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_value`, naming its items; an error refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_unchecked`
  Note over SW: Init the bare repo
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Import the bundle
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Read bundle contents
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Check imported commit
  %%> How:
  %%> - typed data compares the imported commit and tree without a second workspace observation
    Note over SW: Add the waiver lines
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data writes the PR title and body: the caller's body, then each `Docs-unaffected:` line of the proposed body that the body lacks, in the file's order, while the body stays within 65,536 characters
    %%> - the next checks read this text, so the PR gets exactly what they checked; a copy without a pull request skips the step
    Note over SW: Check the environment file
    %%> How:
    %%> - every commit from the copy's start to the candidate must hold the `.env` path exactly as the start does; a commit that adds it, even one a later commit removes, refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_path` before any token exists
    Note over SW: Check the .env content
    %%> How:
    %%> - every object new in the range (file contents, file names, commit messages) and the final pull request title and body, waiver lines included, are searched for the whole `.env` and for each of its values of 8 bytes or more that the start tree does not hold, from the copy's file and from the Gateway's render; a nested-fleet copy's Club key counts as one more value
    %%> - a hit refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_content`, naming the commit and the object, and the file only when its path holds no value; any error refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_unchecked`
    %%> - the range's object digest must equal the one the copy check read, else `tasks.publish_secret_unchecked`: the copy check read the objects this bundle pushes
    Note over SW: Read the .env check
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data reads the check's exit code and its one refusal line from the private scratch, because Swamp keeps no stderr of a failed command step
    %%> - exit 0 passes; a refusal fails the step with that line as its detail; anything else fails with `tasks.publish_secret_unchecked`; a copy mints only after this step and "Read the copy check" succeeded
  SW->>GW: Mint the push token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded `curl` step posts the run id to the Gateway when the push is next; the run id proves the caller
  %%> - the Gateway checks the Operation, the run and the repository, mints a token for that one repository with `contents: write` and `pull_requests: write`, never `workflows`, and writes the two vault values; the reply holds the vault descriptors only
  %%> - no step writes the token into the copy; it receives no credential, in the bundle, the Git configuration or the environment
    SW->>GH: Read the base
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded fetch of the default branch head into the scratch repository, with the minted token as an extra header, so the head is the one at publish time
    %%> - `git merge-base` of the candidate and that head is the checked base; `git rev-list --count candidate..<default>` is `behind_by`
    %%> - the overlapping paths are the paths that both the candidate and the default branch changed since the base
    %%> - the copy's own workflow paths are the paths under `.github/workflows/` that the candidate changed since the merge base (`git diff --name-only <base> candidate`, which is `git diff head...candidate`); a commit that head holds, synced or carried in by hand, is never a change of the copy
    %%> - `git merge-tree --write-tree` merges the two in the repository alone; no checkout and no workspace is touched
    %%> - it also fetches the task branch's tip on origin, when it exists
    %%> - with no own workflow path and a clean merge, it writes a merge commit in the scratch repository when the trees under `.github/workflows/` of the head and the candidate differ: the merge-tree result, parents the candidate then the head, message `Merge main <head sha> at publish` with the default branch's name, author and committer `Orbit <orbit@users.noreply.github.com>`; the push sends it, because GitHub judges the pushed tree against the default branch
    %%> - a republish: a tip that is not an ancestor of the candidate, but an earlier publish merge whose first parent is an ancestor of the candidate and whose second parent is an ancestor of the head, always gets a merge with parents the candidate, the head and that tip, so the push is a fast-forward; a tip whose first two parents already are the candidate and the head is pushed again as it is
    %%> - with no workflow difference and no such tip, it makes no merge and the push sends the candidate
    %%> - a copy's handoff check already merged the default head it judged against (`Merge main <sha> before the check`): when the default branch did not move since that check, `behind_by` is 0 and no merge at publish is needed; the merge at publish stays for a default branch that moved after the check
    %%> - of the intent it reads only `remote`, `base`, `branch` and `node_id`, which the publish intent already had; the candidate is the bundle it imported
    %%> - it writes its statement and exit code to the private scratch; Swamp keeps no stderr of a failed command step
    Note over SW: Check the base
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data reads the statement: `base_commit`, `default_commit`, `behind_by` and `overlapping_paths`, at most 100 paths in at most 3,000 bytes, with `overlapping_more` counting the rest, and `merged_default`, the head of a merge at publish or null
    %%> - an own workflow path fails with `tasks.publish_workflow_change`, naming the paths in the same bounds and the count beyond, before the conflict check and the push: the token has no `workflows` permission
    %%> - it passes the merge commit to the push, when the read made one
    %%> - a conflict of the merge fails with `tasks.publish_conflict`, naming at most 100 conflicting paths in at most 3,000 bytes, so the line fits the 4,096 bytes of detail the Gateway keeps, and the count beyond, before the push; any other error fails with `tasks.publish_failed`
    %%> - a copy pushes only after this step succeeded; a skip of it is never a pass
    %%> - `behind_by` and overlapping paths never refuse on their own
  SW->>GH: Push the branch
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded push without force; authorization is a vault-backed extra header in the environment
  %%> - a task copy's merge at publish is pushed instead of the candidate: `<merge>:refs/heads/task-42`
  Note over SW: Read push result
  %%> How:
  %%> - typed data reads private replies and preserves fast-forward and Workflows refusal codes; for a task copy the Workflows refusal is only a fallback, for a reason the base read did not see
  opt --title and --body
    SW->>GH: Read open PRs
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
    Note over SW: Plan the PR
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data selects an open PR or creation and writes unchanged caller prose into a JSON input file
    %%> - with `--draft` the creation carries `draft: true`; an update of an open PR sends only title and body, so a PR keeps its state
    %%> - for a task copy, a fixed `## Base` section follows the caller's body: the base commit, the default head, how far behind, `- Merged main <sha> at publish` after a merge at publish, and the overlapping paths or none
    %%> - an Orbit marker opens the section, so a caller body that carries an earlier one gets it replaced: a re-publish states it once
    %%> - the section follows the text the .env check read: the caller's body and its waiver lines; the whole stays within 65,536 characters, naming only the count of the paths when their list does not fit
    SW->>GH: Write the PR
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
    Note over SW: Read PR result
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data keeps only the PR number and URL
  end
  SW->>GH: Revoke the token
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded gh api call, only after a token was minted; a refused revoke is best effort and the token expires within an hour
    SW->>N: Discard the copy scratch
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase removes its guest scratch after failure too, once the preflight passed
  Note over SW: Remove local scratch
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded command removes the private worker directory and CLI configuration
  Note over SW: Confirm publication
  %%> How:
  %%> - the native assert requires the push, optional PR reply and worker cleanup to be complete
  alt pushed
    GH-->>SW: Branch pushed · head sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the branch, commit, and the PR number and URL, or null PR fields for a push alone
    %%> - for a task copy also `base_commit`, `default_commit`, `behind_by`, `overlapping_paths`, `overlapping_more` and `merged_default`; `commit` stays the checked candidate after a merge at publish; a run that started on the workflow before the base step has none of them and no `## Base` section
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the publication<br/>branch · commit · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a PR receipt makes the group watch its PR; a branch-only push keeps its workspace
    %%> - a task copy stays until `task:cancel` or the group's end; its group keeps its status
    %%> - Orbit merges no pull request that a task copy's publish opened (`tasks.copy_pr_no_merge`); a person merges it on GitHub
    %%> - task #5165 succeeds
  else a step fails
    GH--xSW: refused or no reply
    %%> When:
    %%> - the workspace moved, the tip diverged, the push or PR write was refused, or a reply was lost
    %%> - a commit of a task copy holds the `.env` Orbit wrote, or the copy's start is gone from the branch history: `tasks.publish_secret_path`; cancel the copy and start the task again
    %%> - a commit of a task copy holds the `.env` content or one of its values under any name: `tasks.publish_secret_content`; remove it from the branch history and check again
    %%> - the content check or the copy check could not run: `tasks.publish_secret_unchecked`; nothing is pushed
    %%> - a commit or the proposed body holds a secret value of the copy or a private key block: `tasks.publish_secret_value`, with `refused` (path:line and secret name) and `refused_more`; nothing is pushed; remove it from the branch history and check again
    %%> - a task copy's candidate changed a path under `.github/workflows/` since the merge base: `tasks.publish_workflow_change`, with the paths in `refused` and `refused_more`; nothing is pushed; a person makes a workflow change of the copy's own in a pull request of their own (docs/reference/tasks.md#the-base-of-a-copy-publish)
    %%> - the task branch's tip is neither an ancestor of the candidate nor an earlier publish merge of it: `tasks.not_fast_forward`; nothing is pushed
    %%> - a task copy's candidate conflicts with the default branch head: `tasks.publish_conflict`, with `conflicting_paths` and `conflicting_more`; nothing is pushed; the `task:merge-round` tick then syncs, merges in one implementer turn, checks, reviews the merge and publishes again (docs/reference/tasks.md#the-merge-round)
    %%> - a step waited 60 s for a behavior lock that another run held: `tasks.publish_lock_timeout`; a step after the push can fail so too, so the branch may be pushed already
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks.push_failed`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>group kept · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5165 fails; group 42 and its workspace stay as they are
    %%> - a publish that the `task:pr-when-done` tick started shows the group's publication as `refused` with this code; the tick does not start the same done check again
    %%> - except `tasks.publish_lock_timeout`: the publication stays `publishing` and the tick starts the done check again, at most 3 attempts in all; a retry is safe, because an identical tip pushes nothing and the PR plan updates an open PR
    %%> On GitHub:
    %%> - a push or PR that started stays; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again: a new task mints a new token at its own push step; an identical tip pushes nothing, and the PR is looked up again before any write
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5165
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    %%> - a copy's `--check` that only pushed names why in `pull_request_withheld`
  end
